window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-724a2ab5c941d08e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prioritize-slack-action-items\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"slack\">整理 Slack 行动项优先级</h1> <p>将 Slack 讨论串和私信整理成有优先级的后续事项队列。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 配合 Slack 和日常工作工具，找出明确请求、隐含的后续事项、已经解决的问题，以及影响最大的下一步行动；先完成梳理，再起草回复或交接内容。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>通过 Slack 接收工作请求、需要区分仍待处理事项和已经解决讨论的人。</li> <li>背景散落在私信、频道和讨论串中的上线、社区、支持、产品和运营工作流。</li> <li>希望先生成有优先级的行动队列，再起草回复、交接内容、文档变更或后续任务的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查找私信、频道、讨论串回复、提及和共享背景，再判断哪些事情仍待处理。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail（需联网）</a></td> <td>当 Slack 讨论提到外联、引荐或已经发送的跟进邮件时，通过邮件交叉核对。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果 Slack 讨论依赖某个文件，阅读相关文档、演示文稿、表格或来源资料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar（需联网）</a></td> <td>当事项涉及会议、上线、网络研讨会或截止日期时，检查日程。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>找出 Slack 中待处理的事项</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请检查 @slack 中与 [workstream] 有关、时间范围为 [time window]，且发给我的消息，并返回一份按优先级排序的行动队列。\n\n请查看私信、群组私信、频道提及和讨论串。\n\n对每一项，请包含：\n- 来源链接或讨论串\n- 对方提出了什么要求\n- 这项工作需要我回复、联系某个人或负责人、修改文档或代码，还是只需要作出决定\n- 这件事为什么重要\n- 建议的下一步\n\n在将事项标记为未解决之前，请先阅读讨论串的最新回复；已经处理的事项不要再列入队列。\n\n不要直接发布消息，只为我起草内容供我审核。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划任务</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"find-the-work-hidden-in-slack\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"slack_1\">找出散落在 Slack 中的工作事项</h2> <p>一项工作请求可能从 Slack 开始，但完整背景往往不在同一处。同事可能在私信中要求回复、在讨论串里说明真正要做什么、在频道里贴出文档链接，之后又在没有再次提到你的情况下解决了问题。</p> <p>这个工作流适用于让 ChatGPT 阅读 Slack 背景、确认请求是否仍然有效，并只返回真正需要你处理的少数事项。目标是得到一份按优先级排序的行动队列：哪些需要回复、作出决定、联系某人、更新文档或交接工作。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-triage-pass\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">执行一次待办梳理</h2> <ol> <li>告诉 ChatGPT 要检查的时间范围、工作主题、人员、频道或关键词。</li> <li>让它搜索私信、群组私信、频道提及和相关讨论串回复。</li> <li>要求它阅读讨论串最近的回复，再判断事项是否仍未解决。</li> <li>让它按紧急程度和影响排序。</li> <li>请它起草回复、交接内容或后续任务。</li> </ol> <p>试用并调整流程后，你可以让 ChatGPT <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">为聊天中的工作安排计划任务</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>，以后按计划重复执行相同梳理。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-for-the-right-output\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">要求合适的输出</h2> <p>有用的待办梳理结果应说明每项工作为何仍待处理，也应排除后来已有人在讨论串中回复过的旧请求。</p> <p>你可能会看到类似这样的结果：</p> <p><strong>最优先事项：</strong> Priya 要的是具体的客户案例，而不只是更多想法。</p> <p><strong>原因：</strong> 团队本周需要在上线更新中加入真实用户，并联系这些用户。</p> <p><strong>依据：</strong> 频道中的原始消息要求提供用例，讨论串后续则说“如果你有潜在线索，请私信我”。</p> <p><strong>下一步：</strong> 回复两位具体的潜在客户线索，或者说明如果更有帮助，你也可以作为案例。</p> <p>好的结果会明确区分：想法不等同于潜在客户线索；仍有效的请求不等同于仅供参考的信息；已经回复的请求不应继续留在队列里。</p> <p>如果结果里噪声太多或可执行事项太少，可以调整提示词；必要时，也可以指定希望 ChatGPT 重点关注的 Slack 频道。</p> <p><a id=\"draft-the-follow-up\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">起草后续内容</h2> <p>行动队列确认无误后，可以在同一聊天中依据刚才收集的证据，让 ChatGPT 起草回复或交接内容：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Draft the Slack reply for each of these action items, using evidence from the triage pass.\n  Do not post it directly, but suggest drafts for my review.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请利用分流排查阶段的证据，为这些行动项分别起草 Slack 回复。\n不要直接发布，只提供草稿供我审阅。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"prioritize-slack-action-items\">Prioritize Slack action items</h1> <p>Turn Slack threads and DMs into a ranked queue of next steps.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with Slack and the tools where work happens to find direct asks, implicit follow-ups, resolved items, and the highest-impact next actions before drafting replies or handoffs.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>People who get work through Slack and need ChatGPT to separate live asks from already-handled chatter.</li> <li>Launch, community, support, product, and operations workstreams where context is split across DMs, channels, and threads.</li> <li>Teams that want a ranked action queue before drafting replies, handoffs, docs changes, or follow-up tasks.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Search DMs, channels, thread replies, mentions, and shared context before deciding what still needs attention.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail (online)</a></td> <td>Cross-check email when a Slack thread refers to an outreach, intro, or sent follow-up.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read linked docs, decks, sheets, or source material when the Slack thread depends on an artifact.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar (online)</a></td> <td>Check event timing when a thread depends on a meeting, launch, webinar, or deadline.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Find What Needs Attention in Slack</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-luna</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Can you check @slack for messages to me about [workstream] from [time window] and return a ranked action queue?\n\nLook across DMs, group DMs, channel mentions, and threads.\n\nFor each item, include:\n- source link or thread\n- what is being asked\n- whether it needs my reply, a person or lead, a docs or code change, or just a decision\n- why it matters\n- the recommended next step\n\nBefore calling anything unresolved, read the latest thread replies and skip items that were already handled.\n\nDo not post messages directly but suggest drafts for my review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444\">Use ChatGPT in Slack</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled tasks</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"find-the-work-hidden-in-slack\">Find the work hidden in Slack</h2> <p>Slack is often where a request starts, but not where the full context lives. A teammate might ask for a reply in a DM, clarify the real action in a thread, link a doc in a channel, and resolve the issue later without mentioning you again.</p> <p>Use this workflow when you want ChatGPT to read the Slack context, check whether the ask is still live, and return the few items that actually need your attention. The goal is to get a ranked action queue: what needs a reply, a decision, a person to contact, a doc update, or a handoff.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-triage-pass\">Run the triage pass</h2> <ol> <li>Give ChatGPT a time window, workstream, person, channel, or topic.</li> <li>Ask it to search DMs, group DMs, channel mentions, and relevant thread replies.</li> <li>Have ChatGPT read the latest thread tail before calling an item unresolved.</li> <li>Ask for a ranked queue sorted by urgency and impact.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to draft the reply, handoff, or follow-up task.</li> </ol> <p>After trying this and tweaking the flow to match your needs, you can <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations#schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">schedule a task for the work from the chat</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/automations/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> by asking ChatGPT to do the same thing on a schedule.</p> <h2 id=\"ask-for-the-right-output\">Ask for the right output</h2> <p>A useful triage result should explain why each item is still live. It should also skip old asks that someone answered later in the thread.</p> <p>You should expect to see something like this:</p> <p><strong>Top action item:</strong> Priya is asking for concrete customer examples, not just more ideas.</p> <pre><code>**Why it matters:** the launch update needs real people the\nteam can contact this week.\n\n\n\n\n**Evidence:** the original channel message asked for use cases,\nbut the thread later says \"please DM me if you have leads.\"\n\n\n\n\n**Next step:** reply with two named leads, or say you can be\nthe example if that is more useful.\n</code></pre> <p>Good output makes the distinction explicit: an idea is different from a lead, a live ask is different from an FYI, and a request you already answered shouldn't stay in the queue.</p> <p>If you get too much noise or too few actionable items, tweak the prompt and if needed, mention specific slack channels you want ChatGPT to pay attention to.</p> <h2 id=\"draft-the-follow-up\">Draft the follow-up</h2> <p>Once the queue is right, keep the action in the same chat. Ask ChatGPT to draft a reply or handoff from the evidence it already gathered:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Draft the Slack reply for each of these action items, using evidence from the triage pass.\n  Do not post it directly, but suggest drafts for my review.\n</code></pre>"};
